Note: this licence covers what this repository adds: the driver, the scripts
and the documents under waterbox/, docs/ and .github/. waterbox/driver/memfs.cc
and memfs.h come from chimera-core-vita3k, by the same author under the same
licence.

The patches/ directory changes Xenia Canary
(https://github.com/xenia-canary/xenia-canary) and is offered under Xenia's
terms, BSD-3-Clause (extern/xenia/LICENSE).

The built package, xenia.chimeraCore, contains Xenia Canary and the
libraries it links. Two of them are LGPL-2.1: Xenia's fork of FFmpeg and
libmspack's LZX decoder. The rest are permissive or public domain.
waterbox/package-licenses.json names every component, its licence and its
exact source, and the package carries the licence texts. The package
contains no game, no system software and no key.
